            <ArticleTitle>Pain management in the orthopedic patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>73-87</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain is a familiar phenomenon to all orthopedic nurses. As Dunwoody said, &quot;Few things we do for patients are more fundamental to the quality of life than relieving pain.&quot; We as orthopedic nurses are in a position to contribute to the positive management of pain by using a comprehensive approach to pain management that involves the participation of the patient. We need to believe the patient's pain, try new approaches, and help our patients achieve pain relief.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
